1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,467
Cities already record hours of street video.

2
00:00:03,979 --> 00:00:07,410
ViZ Agent watches it, so city engineers don't
have to.

3
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:11,827
San Francisco pledged Vision Zero in 2014.

4
00:00:12,348 --> 00:00:16,013
Twelve years later, serious crashes are higher,
not lower.

5
00:00:16,403 --> 00:00:21,203
A new city law now asks for progress reports
every quarter.

6
00:00:21,706 --> 00:00:25,592
The close calls are already on camera. Nobody
has time to watch them.

7
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:29,241
So we built an agent that does the watching.

8
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:33,536
It searches the indexed video for four kinds of
pedestrian conflict.

9
00:00:34,023 --> 00:00:37,669
Every candidate must pass three independent
checks before it counts.

10
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:41,732
Then it ranks the locations and drafts a fix for
the worst one.

11
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:49,664
In our live run, the sweep pulled sixty
candidate clips from a Toronto dashcam and four
San Francisco street cameras.

12
00:00:50,002 --> 00:00:51,863
Fifty-six were thrown out.

13
00:00:52,285 --> 00:00:55,432
So an engineer reviews four clips, not sixty.

14
00:00:56,610 --> 00:01:01,570
What survives is grouped by camera, so the worst
location rises to the top.

15
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:06,970
This is one of the verified clips, straight from
a San Francisco street camera.

16
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:14,802
For a second opinion, Cosmos Reason watches the
clip again and explains what physically
happened.

17
00:01:15,504 --> 00:01:18,303
It agrees: this is a real conflict.

18
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:23,448
An engineer confirms or rejects each clip with
one click.

19
00:01:23,874 --> 00:01:28,510
Those labels measure the agent's precision and
become a dataset for the next model.

20
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:32,174
Approved clips turn into a drafted work order.

21
00:01:32,727 --> 00:01:38,610
The cause of the conflict picks a proven federal
safety fix, ready to file with SF311.

22
00:01:39,217 --> 00:01:42,470
A person still signs off before anything is
sent.

23
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:50,431
Every search, check and model call is traced in
Weights & Biases Weave, so each decision can be
audited.

24
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:55,452
Less time watching video. More time fixing
streets.

25
00:01:55,844 --> 00:01:59,034
Built by Team 20 for the VAST Builders
Challenge.
